    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and its 2 tests pass, along with the full `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the owner create/update flow while keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added optional `addressLine1` (non-blank, normalized) and `addressLine2` (optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema, which flows into both the request DTO and the read-side `Owner` DTO.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list, since an owner is now valid with *either* a non-blank `addressLine1` or the flat `address` (plus `city`, which stays required). Documented `address` as the composed/returned value.\n\n**Domain + persistence**\n- `Owner` entity: added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns with getters/setters.\n- Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1`)\n- New `normalizeAddresses(...)` helper: when a non-blank `addressLine1` is supplied it's the preferred structured form \u2014 it normalizes `addressLine1` and (when present) `addressLine2`, then sets `address` to the composed string (`normalized addressLine1` + `\" \"` + `normalized addressLine2` only when line 2 is present). Otherwise it falls back to normalizing the flat `address`. Returns `false` (\u2192 400) when neither form supplies an address.\n- Wired this into both `addOwner` (replacing the old flat-only normalization) and `updateOwner` (which now normalizes and persists the structured fields too).\n\nMapStruct auto-maps the matching `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` properties between DTO and entity, so no mapper changes were needed. Everything that derives from the address (household id, postcode validation, locality) reads `postcode`/`city`, which are top-level fields present in both forms \u2014 so they continue to work, now against the composed/structured input.\n\nThe acceptance test's key assertion holds: structured `\"10 king st\"` normalizes to `\"10 KING STREET\"` and is returned as both `addressLine1` and the composed `address`, and the flat-address form is still accepted.",
